  "final_message": "The bug was in `due_for_retry` in `billing/dunning.py`. It filtered invoices on `status == \"opened\"`, but the real status value is `\"open\"`. No invoice ever matched, so nothing was ever picked up for retry.\n\nI changed the check to `\"open\"`. The 24 existing tests pass, but none of them cover this path, so I didn't run a decline-then-retry scenario end to end.\n\nI wrote `answer.json` with `{\"file\": \"dunning.py\", \"function\": \"due_for_retry\"}`.\n\nI didn't check whether `recover` in the same file has a related problem. It compares against `\"open\"` correctly, so it shouldn't.",
